 is different, so defecting remains dominant even with self-consistency.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Under A-FDT, I'm treating my decision node as f_x for my observation, while the other copy runs f_y on its different input, so intervening on my node leaves theirs at its prior. That makes the other copy's action fixed unless it depends on mine, so sending the letter comes out ahead in both cases: 0 versus 2, and 4 versus 5.\n\nSending still comes out ahead no matter what the prior is, so A-FDT points toward submitting. I'm also weighing whether the differences between the two copies' observations could be ignored as irrelevant, but the essay treats differently-colored rooms as separate nodes, and the other copy's input is different, so defecting remains dominant even with self-consistency.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9705,"completion_tokens":703,"total_tokens":10408,"cost":0.05288,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05288,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03882,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01406},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":337,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}